+ * the D3D12 renderer's write-back). Each R32F / R32G32B32A32F target of at
+ * most RSX_ENGINE_FLOAT_WRITEBACK texels (default 4096; 0 = off) that was drawn
+ * since its last store is read back at the flip and stored big-endian at its
+ * own pitch -- one flip of latency, as the console's CPU sees it after the
+ * frame. Only targets written since their last store: a stale one would
