+ * does: an operand with biased exponent 0 (any fraction) is an SPU zero and becomes +0 before the
+ * op; a result below 2^-126 flushes to +0 (the SPU truncates toward zero, and a double result below
+ * 2^-126 is below it exactly: 2^-126 is a double, so rounding cannot cross it from above, and a
+ * double fma that rounds up onto it lands on a 24-bit boundary, which the err check already sends
+ * to the exact path). Before this, every denormal operand or tiny result took the per-lane exact
+ * path -- audio filters whose state decays toward zero (libsynth2's reverb / filter loops) ran
+ * most of their fa / fm / fma there, and synth2 went from ~30% to ~95% of a core.
